{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def remove_Occ(input_string: str, target_char: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes the first and last occurrence of a given character from the string.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = input_string.find(target_char)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        # Character not found, return the original string.\n        return input_string\n\n    last_idx = input_string.rfind(target_char)\n\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        # Only one occurrence of the character, remove it.\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx + 1:]\n    else:\n        # Multiple occurrences, remove the first and the last.\n        # First, remove the character at first_idx.\n        string_after_first_removal = input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx + 1:]\n        \n        # The last_idx in the original string now corresponds to (last_idx - 1)\n        # in string_after_first_removal, as a character before it was removed.\n        new_last_idx = last_idx - 1\n        return string_after_first_removal[:new_last_idx] + string_after_first_removal[new_last_idx + 1:]"}
