{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the Bell number for the given input parameter.\n\n    This represents the number of ways to partition a set with n elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Memoization table for Stirling numbers of the second kind S(n, k)\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _stirling_number_second_kind(n_val: int, k_val: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates Stirling number of the second kind S(n_val, k_val).\"\"\"\n        if (n_val, k_val) in memo:\n            return memo[(n_val, k_val)]\n\n        # Base cases\n        if k_val < 0 or k_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if k_val == 0:\n            return 1 if n_val == 0 else 0  # S(0,0)=1, S(n,0)=0 for n>0\n        if k_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n\n        # Recurrence relation: S(n, k) = S(n-1, k-1) + k * S(n-1, k)\n        result = (_stirling_number_second_kind(n_val - 1, k_val - 1) +\n                  k_val * _stirling_number_second_kind(n_val - 1, k_val))\n        \n        memo[(n_val, k_val)] = result\n        return result\n\n    total_bell_number = 0\n    # Bell number B_n = sum_{k=0 to n} S(n, k)\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        total_bell_number += _stirling_number_second_kind(n, k)\n    \n    return total_bell_number"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the Bell number for given integer n.\n    This implementation uses dynamic programming to build a Bell triangle.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _create_bell_triangle(max_n: int) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Create Bell triangle up to row max_n using a dynamic programming approach.\"\"\"\n        bell_triangle = []\n\n        # Initialize the first row for B(0)\n        # B(0) = 1 (partition of an empty set is 1 way: the empty partition)\n        bell_triangle.append([1])\n\n        # Generate subsequent rows of the Bell triangle\n        for i in range(1, max_n + 1):\n            prev_row = bell_triangle[-1]\n            current_row = []\n            \n            # The first element of the current row is the last element of the previous row\n            current_row.append(prev_row[-1])\n            \n            # Compute subsequent elements using the recurrence relation:\n            # T(i, j) = T(i-1, j-1) + T(i, j-1)\n            for j in range(1, i + 1):\n                current_row.append(current_row[-1] + prev_row[j-1])\n            \n            bell_triangle.append(current_row)\n        return bell_triangle\n\n    # The Bell number B(n) is the first element of the n-th row of the Bell triangle.\n    # Note: For n=0, _create_bell_triangle(0) will return [[1]], and bell_triangle[0][0] is 1.\n    bell_triangle = _create_bell_triangle(n)\n    return bell_triangle[n][0]"}
