{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "def index_minimum(tuple_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value.\n    Handles an empty list by returning None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return None\n\n    # Initialize with the first tuple's values\n    min_first_value = tuple_list[0][0]\n    min_second_value = tuple_list[0][1]\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the list to find the minimum\n    for item in tuple_list[1:]:\n        current_first_value = item[0]\n        current_second_value = item[1]\n\n        if current_second_value < min_second_value:\n            min_second_value = current_second_value\n            min_first_value = current_first_value\n\n    return min_first_value"}
