{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    The result is 0 if m < 0 or m >= n based on definition.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _combinations(N: int, K: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(N, K).\"\"\"\n        if K < 0 or K > N:\n            return 0\n        if K == 0 or K == N:\n            return 1\n        # Optimize K for smaller calculation (C(N, K) = C(N, N-K))\n        if K > N // 2:\n            K = N - K\n        \n        res = 1\n        for i in range(K):\n            res = res * (N - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # The Eulerian number A(n, m) is 0 for m < 0 or m >= n.\n    # The formula naturally handles m >= n.\n    # For m < 0, range(m + 1) will be an empty range, resulting in 0, which is correct.\n    for j in range(m + 1):\n        term = ((-1)**j) * _combinations(n + 1, j) * ((m + 1 - j)**n)\n        total_sum += term\n\n    return total_sum"}
