{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(arr: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in an array of integers.\n    Handles edge cases for all zeroes or no zeroes in the array.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _count_zeros(data: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of zero elements in the given list.\"\"\"\n        return data.count(0)\n\n    def _count_non_zeros(data: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of non-zero elements in the given list.\"\"\"\n        return len(data) - data.count(0)\n\n    def _calculate_ratio(zeros: int, non_zeros: int) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes, handling division by zero.\"\"\"\n        if non_zeros == 0:\n            return float('inf')\n        return float(zeros) / non_zeros\n\n    num_zeros = _count_zeros(arr)\n    num_non_zeros = _count_non_zeros(arr)\n\n    return _calculate_ratio(num_zeros, num_non_zeros)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number can be represented as a sum of distinct non-zero powers of 2.\n    This is true for any positive even integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n    \n    # A positive number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2\n    # (i.e., 2^k where k >= 1) if and only if it is an even number.\n    # An odd number requires 2^0 (which is 1) in its binary representation,\n    # and 2^0 is not considered a non-zero power of 2.\n    return number % 2 == 0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def _generate_powers_of_two(max_value: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Generates a list of non-zero powers of two up to max_value.\"\"\"\n    powers = []\n    current_power = 2  # Start with 2^1\n    while current_power <= max_value:\n        powers.append(current_power)\n        current_power *= 2\n    return powers\ndef _check_sum_representation(target: int, powers: list[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if target is representable as sum of non-zero powers of two.\n    Any positive even integer satisfies this condition mathematically.\"\"\"\n    return target > 0 and target % 2 == 0\ndef is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks whether the given number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2.\"\"\"\n    # Negative or zero numbers cannot be represented as a sum of positive powers.\n    if n <= 0:\n        return False\n    \n    # Generate powers of two (this list is conceptually passed to _check_sum_representation).\n    powers_list = _generate_powers_of_two(n)\n    \n    # The actual check relies on the mathematical property of such sums.\n    return _check_sum_representation(n, powers_list)"}
