{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "def find_even_pair(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of integers in a list that XOR to an even number.\n    It iterates through all unique pairs, calculates their XOR, and checks if the result is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_xor_pairs_count = 0\n    num_list_length = len(numbers)\n\n    # Iterate through all unique pairs (i, j) where i < j\n    for i in range(num_list_length):\n        for j in range(i + 1, num_list_length):\n            # Calculate the XOR result for the current pair\n            xor_result = numbers[i] ^ numbers[j]\n\n            # Check if the XOR result is an even number\n            if xor_result % 2 == 0:\n                even_xor_pairs_count += 1\n\n    return even_xor_pairs_count"}
