{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array, n, element):\n    # Helper function to find the first occurrence of an element using binary search.\n    def binary_search_first(arr, target, low, high):\n        first_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                first_idx = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return first_idx\n\n    # Helper function to find the last occurrence of an element using binary search.\n    def binary_search_last(arr, target, low, high):\n        last_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                last_idx = mid\n                low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return last_idx\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_occurrence = binary_search_first(array, element, 0, n - 1)\n\n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_occurrence == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_occurrence = binary_search_last(array, element, 0, n - 1)\n\n    # Calculate the total count of occurrences of the element.\n    count = last_occurrence - first_occurrence + 1\n\n    # Check if the count is greater than n/2.\n    return count > n / 2"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    def _binary_search_first(arr, target, low, high):\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of target in arr.\"\"\"\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:  # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    def _binary_search_last(arr, target, low, high):\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of target in arr.\"\"\"\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:  # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    first_idx = _binary_search_first(array, element, 0, n - 1)\n\n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _binary_search_last(array, element, 0, n - 1)\n\n    # Calculate the total count of the element.\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    # Check if the count is strictly greater than n/2.\n    return count > (n // 2)"}
