{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming to build up solutions for substrings.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence\n    # for the substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromic subsequences of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the dp table for gaps of length 1 to n-1\n    for gap in range(1, n):\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            j = i + gap\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters match, add 2 to the LPS of the inner substring\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + (dp[i + 1][j - 1] if i + 1 <= j - 1 else 0)\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, take the maximum of\n                # LPS of s[i+1...j] and s[i...j-1]\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    # The result for the entire string s[0...n-1] is in dp[0][n-1]\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming with O(n^2) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence\n    # for the substring s[i...j].\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substring lengths from 2 to n.\n    for current_length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - current_length + 1):\n            j = i + current_length - 1  # j is the end index of the current substring\n\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters at ends match, they contribute 2 to the length,\n                # plus the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1] if current_length > 2 else 2\n            else:\n                # If characters at ends do not match, take the maximum of\n                # excluding s[i] (LPS of s[i+1...j]) or excluding s[j] (LPS of s[i...j-1]).\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    # The result is the length of the LPS for the entire string s[0...n-1].\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
