{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\ndef convert(input_number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Convert a complex number to polar coordinates.\n\n    Args:\n        input_number: int, float, or complex number\n\n    Returns:\n        tuple: (magnitude: float, angle: float)\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(input_number, complex):\n        real_part = input_number.real\n        imag_part = input_number.imag\n    else:\n        # Treat int/float as a complex number with zero imaginary part\n        real_part = float(input_number)\n        imag_part = 0.0\n\n    magnitude = math.sqrt(real_part**2 + imag_part**2)\n    angle = math.atan2(imag_part, real_part)\n\n    return (magnitude, angle)"}
