{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\ndef convert(input) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a numeric input (int, float, or complex) to polar coordinates.\n    Returns a tuple containing the magnitude and angle in radians.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _normalize_input(val) -> complex:\n        \"\"\"Converts the input value to a complex number.\"\"\"\n        if isinstance(val, (int, float)):\n            return complex(val, 0)\n        return val\n\n    def _calculate_magnitude(z: complex) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the magnitude of a complex number.\"\"\"\n        return math.sqrt(z.real**2 + z.imag**2)\n\n    def _calculate_angle(z: complex) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the angle (in radians) of a complex number.\"\"\"\n        return math.atan2(z.imag, z.real)\n\n    normalized_z = _normalize_input(input)\n    magnitude = _calculate_magnitude(normalized_z)\n    angle = _calculate_angle(normalized_z)\n\n    return (magnitude, angle)"}
