{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers less than the given non-negative number.\n    Uses an internal helper function to check for primality.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a given number is prime.\"\"\"\n        if n <= 1:\n            return False\n        if n <= 3:  # 2 and 3 are prime numbers\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    count = 0\n    for num in range(2, number):\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
