{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "import math\ndef _validate_input(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Ensures the input number is non-negative. Returns True if valid.\"\"\"\n    return number >= 0\ndef _is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime using trial division up to its square root. Handles edge cases for 0, 1, and 2.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\ndef count_Primes_nums(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts prime numbers less than the given non-negative integer. Iterates and uses _is_prime for each number.\"\"\"\n    _validate_input(number) # Validate input as per design; constraints prevent error handling if invalid.\n\n    prime_count = 0\n    for i in range(2, number):\n        if _is_prime(i):\n            prime_count += 1\n    return prime_count"}
