{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Maximizes elements of two tuples containing nested numeric tuples.\n\n    Compares corresponding nested tuples element-wise and returns a new tuple\n    with the maximum values at each position.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _get_maximum(value1, value2):\n        \"\"\"Helper to select the maximum value from two inputs.\"\"\"\n        return max(value1, value2)\n\n    result_elements = []\n    # Iterate through corresponding nested tuples from both input tuples\n    for sub_tuple1, sub_tuple2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        maximized_sub_tuple_elements = []\n        # For each pair of nested tuples, maximize their individual elements\n        for element1, element2 in zip(sub_tuple1, sub_tuple2):\n            maximized_sub_tuple_elements.append(_get_maximum(element1, element2))\n        result_elements.append(tuple(maximized_sub_tuple_elements))\n    \n    return tuple(result_elements)"}
