{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into n sublists by distributing elements cyclically.\n    Elements are distributed in a round-robin fashion across the sublists.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize n empty sublists. If n is 0 or negative, this creates an empty list of lists.\n    # It is assumed that n will be a positive integer based on the assert example.\n    result = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Iterate through the input list with index and value\n    for index, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        # Determine which sublist the current element belongs to using modulo\n        target_sublist_index = index % n\n        # Append the element to the determined sublist\n        result[target_sublist_index].append(item)\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/267", "solution": "def square_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the squares of the first n odd natural numbers.\n    The sum is computed using the direct mathematical formula.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n    # The sum of squares of the first n odd numbers is given by the formula:\n    # n * (2n - 1) * (2n + 1) / 3\n    # Since n, (2n-1), and (2n+1) are integers, and their product is always divisible by 3,\n    # integer division can be used safely.\n    return n * (2 * n - 1) * (2 * n + 1) // 3"}
