{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef list_split(input_list: List, n: int) -> List[List]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits an input list into n sublists using a cyclic distribution pattern.\n    Elements are distributed such that each sublist contains every nth element,\n    starting from sequential offset positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        # As per design context and prompt, assume n is a positive integer.\n        # If n is 0 or negative, it's an edge case not explicitly requiring\n        # error handling or special return values beyond what the loop naturally does.\n        # An empty list of lists is a reasonable default for n=0\n        # or if one interpreted n=0 as \"no splits\".\n        return [[] for _ in range(n)] if n > 0 else []\n\n    # Initialize n empty sublists\n    result_lists: List[List] = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Distribute elements cyclically\n    for index, element in enumerate(input_list):\n        sublist_index = index % n\n        result_lists[sublist_index].append(element)\n\n    return result_lists"}
