{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def _count_digit_frequencies(number: int) -> dict[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"Counts frequency of each digit in the number.\"\"\"\n    s_number = str(number)\n    frequencies = {}\n    for digit_char in s_number:\n        frequencies[digit_char] = frequencies.get(digit_char, 0) + 1\n    return frequencies\ndef _check_frequency_rule(digit: str, frequency: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if digit frequency satisfies the rule frequency <= digit_value.\"\"\"\n    digit_value = int(digit)\n    return frequency <= digit_value\ndef validate(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    digit_frequencies = _count_digit_frequencies(number)\n\n    for digit_char, freq in digit_frequencies.items():\n        if not _check_frequency_rule(digit_char, freq):\n            return False\n    return True"}
