{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(integer: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in an integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    Handles both positive and negative integers by using their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _process_integer(num: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Converts an integer to its absolute string representation.\"\"\"\n        return str(abs(num))\n\n    def _count_digit_frequencies(num_str: str) -> dict[str, int]:\n        \"\"\"Counts the frequency of each digit in a string.\"\"\"\n        frequencies = {}\n        for digit_char in num_str:\n            frequencies[digit_char] = frequencies.get(digit_char, 0) + 1\n        return frequencies\n\n    num_str = _process_integer(integer)\n    frequencies = _count_digit_frequencies(num_str)\n\n    for digit_char, frequency in frequencies.items():\n        digit_value = int(digit_char)\n        if frequency > digit_value:\n            return False\n    return True"}
