{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "def large_product(list1, list2, count):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the specified number of largest products from two lists, selecting one factor from each.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_products = []\n    for num1 in list1:\n        for num2 in list2:\n            all_products.append(num1 * num2)\n\n    all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return all_products[:count]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(array, length, i, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from the prefix until the ith index\n    and also including the given kth element, where k > i.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at array[j]\n    # within the prefix array[0...i].\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    # Calculate the maximum sum increasing subsequence for the prefix array[0...i]\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        # Base case: subsequence containing only array[j]\n        dp[j] = array[j] \n\n        # Check previous elements (x < j) to extend the subsequence\n        for x in range(j):\n            if array[j] > array[x]:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[x] + array[j])\n    \n    # array[k] is the element that must be included.\n    # We need to find the maximum sum from dp[j] such that array[j] < array[k].\n    # Initialize to 0 to handle cases where no prefix element can precede array[k]\n    # (i.e., array[k] is the smallest element or smaller than all prefix elements).\n    max_prefix_sum_before_k = 0 \n\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if array[j] < array[k]:\n            max_prefix_sum_before_k = max(max_prefix_sum_before_k, dp[j])\n            \n    # The total maximum sum is the maximum sum from the prefix (that ends with an element \n    # less than array[k]) plus the value of array[k] itself.\n    return max_prefix_sum_before_k + array[k]"}
