{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum for a given integer n using a recursive formula with memoization.\n    f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n: int) -> int:\n        # Base case: if current_n is 1 or less, return current_n itself.\n        if current_n <= 1:\n            return current_n\n        \n        # If the result for current_n is already memoized, return it.\n        if current_n in memo:\n            return memo[current_n]\n\n        # Calculate the sum of recursive calls for n/2, n/3, n/4, and n/5 using integer division.\n        sum_of_parts = (\n            _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n // 2) +\n            _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n // 3) +\n            _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n // 4) +\n            _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n // 5)\n        )\n        \n        # The result is the maximum of the sum of parts and the current_n itself.\n        result = max(sum_of_parts, current_n)\n        \n        # Store the computed result in the memoization cache before returning.\n        memo[current_n] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _calculate_max_sum_recursive(n)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/391", "solution": "def convert_list_dictionary(list1, list2, list3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts three parallel lists into a list of nested dictionaries.\n    Each element from list1 becomes an outer key, list2 an inner key, and list3 an inner value.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (len(list1) == len(list2) == len(list3)):\n        raise ValueError(\"All input lists must have the same length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        outer_key = list1[i]\n        inner_key = list2[i]\n        inner_value = list3[i]\n        result.append({outer_key: {inner_key: inner_value}})\n    return result"}
