{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum using the recursive equation f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Memoization is used to optimize performance for repeated calculations.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def calculate_recursive_sum(current_n: int) -> int:\n        if current_n <= 1:\n            return current_n\n        if current_n in memo:\n            return memo[current_n]\n\n        sum_of_parts = (\n            calculate_recursive_sum(current_n // 2) +\n            calculate_recursive_sum(current_n // 3) +\n            calculate_recursive_sum(current_n // 4) +\n            calculate_recursive_sum(current_n // 5)\n        )\n        \n        result = max(sum_of_parts, current_n)\n        memo[current_n] = result\n        return result\n\n    return calculate_recursive_sum(n)"}
