{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "def Find_Min(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a given list of sublists.\n    Returns an empty list if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    min_sublist = input_list[0]\n    min_length = len(input_list[0])\n\n    for sublist in input_list:\n        current_length = len(sublist)\n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            min_sublist = sublist\n            \n    return min_sublist"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "def Find_Min(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a list of sublists.\n    Returns the first such sublist encountered if multiple have the same minimum length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    min_sublist = None\n\n    for sublist in input_list:\n        current_length = len(sublist)\n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            min_sublist = sublist\n            \n    return min_sublist"}
