{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def tuple_intersection(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the tuple intersection of elements in two tuple lists,\n    considering tuples with the same elements but different orders as equivalent.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Utility function to convert a tuple to a normalized, comparable form.\n    def normalize_tuple(t):\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n\n    # Create a mapping from normalized tuples to their original forms from list1.\n    # This ensures we retain the specific original tuple from list1 if a match is found.\n    normalized_to_original_map1 = {}\n    for original_tuple in list1:\n        normalized_form = normalize_tuple(original_tuple)\n        if normalized_form not in normalized_to_original_map1:\n            normalized_to_original_map1[normalized_form] = original_tuple\n\n    # Create a set of normalized tuples from list2 for efficient membership testing.\n    normalized_forms_in_list2 = set()\n    for t2 in list2:\n        normalized_forms_in_list2.add(normalize_tuple(t2))\n\n    # Identify common normalized forms and collect the corresponding original tuples from list1.\n    intersection_result = set()\n    for normalized_form_from_list1 in normalized_to_original_map1:\n        if normalized_form_from_list1 in normalized_forms_in_list2:\n            intersection_result.add(normalized_to_original_map1[normalized_form_from_list1])\n\n    return intersection_result"}
