{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "def two_unique_nums(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes duplicate numbers from a list, returning only numbers that appear exactly once.\n    The original order of unique numbers is preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    # Step 1: Count occurrences of each number\n    counts = {}\n    for num in input_list:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    # Step 2: Filter numbers that appear exactly once, preserving original order\n    result = []\n    for num in input_list:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            result.append(num)\n\n    return result"}
