{"task_id": "Mbpp/615", "solution": "def average_tuple(tuple_of_tuples: tuple) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the average for each inner tuple in a tuple of tuples.\n    Returns a list of these averages as floats.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _calculate_average(inner_tuple: tuple) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Computes the arithmetic mean of elements within a single tuple.\"\"\"\n        if not inner_tuple:\n            return 0.0  # Handle empty inner tuples gracefully as per common average conventions\n        return sum(inner_tuple) / len(inner_tuple)\n\n    def _format_result(value: float) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the calculated value is represented as a float.\"\"\"\n        return float(value)\n\n    averages = []\n    for inner_tuple in tuple_of_tuples:\n        raw_average = _calculate_average(inner_tuple)\n        formatted_average = _format_result(raw_average)\n        averages.append(formatted_average)\n    return averages"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/615", "solution": "def average_tuple(input_tuples: tuple) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the average value for each inner tuple in a tuple of tuples.\n    Returns a list of these floating-point averages.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for inner_tuple in input_tuples:\n        # Sum the elements of the inner tuple and divide by its length to get the average.\n        # It's assumed inner tuples are non-empty based on problem constraints.\n        results.append(sum(inner_tuple) / len(inner_tuple))\n    return results"}
