{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "def largest_subset(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest subset of numbers where every pair is divisible.\n    The function generates all possible subsets and checks the divisibility condition for each.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Sort the input numbers. This helps in validating subsets efficiently later,\n    # as elements within a valid divisible subset must also be in increasing order.\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n\n    def is_valid_subset(subset: list[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if every pair in a given subset is divisible.\n        Assumes the input subset is already sorted in ascending order.\n        \"\"\"\n        if len(subset) <= 1:\n            return True\n        \n        # For a sorted subset (s_1, s_2, ..., s_k), if s_i % s_{i-1} == 0 for all i,\n        # then by transitivity, s_j % s_i == 0 for any j > i.\n        # Thus, checking adjacent elements is sufficient.\n        for i in range(1, len(subset)):\n            if subset[i] % subset[i-1] != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def generate_all_subsets(nums: list[int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Generates all non-empty subsets of a given list of numbers.\n        The order of elements in generated subsets will match their order in `nums`.\n        \"\"\"\n        all_subsets = []\n        n = len(nums)\n        # Iterate through all possible combinations using bit manipulation.\n        for i in range(1 << n): # (1 << n) is equivalent to 2^n\n            current_subset = []\n            for j in range(n):\n                # If the j-th bit is set in i, include the j-th element from nums.\n                if (i >> j) & 1:\n                    current_subset.append(nums[j])\n            if current_subset: # Only add non-empty subsets to the list.\n                all_subsets.append(current_subset)\n        return all_subsets\n\n    # Generate all non-empty subsets from the sorted input list.\n    all_possible_subsets = generate_all_subsets(sorted_numbers)\n    \n    max_size = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through all generated subsets to find the largest valid one.\n    for subset in all_possible_subsets:\n        if is_valid_subset(subset):\n            max_size = max(max_size, len(subset))\n            \n    return max_size"}
