{"task_id": "Mbpp/740", "solution": "def tuple_to_dict(input_tuple: tuple) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple into a key-value dictionary using adjacent elements.\n    Raises ValueError if the input tuple has an odd number of elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _validate_tuple_length(t: tuple) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that the tuple has an even number of elements.\"\"\"\n        if len(t) % 2 != 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Tuple must have an even number of elements to form key-value pairs.\")\n\n    def _create_pairs(t: tuple) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Creates a list of (key, value) pairs from adjacent tuple elements.\"\"\"\n        return list(zip(t[::2], t[1::2]))\n\n    def _build_dictionary(pairs: list) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Constructs a dictionary from a list of key-value pairs.\"\"\"\n        return dict(pairs)\n\n    _validate_tuple_length(input_tuple)\n    pairs = _create_pairs(input_tuple)\n    return _build_dictionary(pairs)"}
