{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    The original list remains unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the effective number of rotations\n    # This handles cases where positions > n or positions = 0\n    effective_positions = positions % n\n\n    # Slice the list into two parts and concatenate them\n    # The last 'effective_positions' elements move to the front\n    return lst[n - effective_positions:] + lst[:n - effective_positions]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Returns a new list with the elements rotated.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    n = len(lst)\n    # Calculate the effective number of rotations using modulo.\n    k = positions % n\n    \n    # Perform the rotation using slicing and concatenation.\n    return lst[-k:] + lst[:-k]"}
