{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "def count_reverse_pairs(strings: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unique pairs of reverse strings in the given list.\n    Palindromic strings are not counted as pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    pairs_count = 0\n    # A set to keep track of indices of strings already counted in a pair.\n    counted_indices = set() \n\n    n = len(strings)\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i in counted_indices:\n            continue\n\n        s1 = strings[i]\n        rev_s1 = s1[::-1]\n\n        # Palindromes cannot form a reverse pair with another distinct string.\n        if s1 == rev_s1:\n            continue\n\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if j in counted_indices:\n                continue\n\n            s2 = strings[j]\n\n            if s2 == rev_s1:\n                pairs_count += 1\n                counted_indices.add(i)\n                counted_indices.add(j)\n                # Once a pair is found for s1, move to the next potential s1.\n                break \n    return pairs_count"}
