{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(array, target_value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in a sorted array.\n    Returns the index where the target_value can be inserted to maintain sorted order,\n    ensuring it's placed after any existing equal elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    \n    # Initialize 'ans' to n, which is the correct insertion point if target_value\n    # is greater than all elements in the array or if the array is empty.\n    ans = n \n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        \n        if array[mid] <= target_value:\n            # If array[mid] is less than or equal to the target, the insertion point\n            # must be to the right of mid. We discard mid and the left half.\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            # If array[mid] is greater than the target, mid is a potential insertion\n            # point. We store it and try to find an even smaller index in the left half.\n            ans = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n            \n    return ans"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/787", "solution": "import re\ndef text_match_three(text):\n    # Matches strings containing 'a' followed by exactly three 'b's.\n    # The (?!b) ensures that the 'bbb' is not followed by another 'b'.\n    pattern = r\"a[b]{3}(?!b)\"\n    return re.search(pattern, text) is not None"}
